# Temperature sensor
# Level 3 - Sensors and motors
#
# Read a TMP36 temperature sensor and print the temperature in degrees Celsius.
# You learn: volts, temperatures (C), smooth() for steady readings and round().
# You need: a TMP36 (flat side towards you): left leg to 5V, middle leg to A0, right leg to GND.

board uno

sensor = analog A0

every 500 ms:
    # The TMP36 gives 0.5 V at 0 C and 1.5 V at 100 C: scale() does the maths.
    var t = scale(smooth(sensor.volts, 10), 0.5 V..1.5 V, 0 C..100 C)
    print "Temperature: {round(t, 1)}"
    plot t
